From: port_ios lavender
Subject: [PATCH 0325] lavender: zero-copy scanout surfaces, fast panel copy, 60 Hz vsync pacing, 370/465 MHz GPU clock

1. Reserve an early physically-contiguous WB scanout pool (up to 5 x 12 MiB)
   in SweetSurface for lavender full-screen surfaces, matching topaz geometry.
2. Add kLavSurfaceInfo (6) and kLavSurfaceSync (7) on LavenderGPUUserClient so
   LavenderMetal renders directly into contiguous IOSurfaces (0 ms sync copy)
   using real sweet_dcache_clean / sweet_dcache_flush maintenance.
3. Optimize SweetFramebuffer::present() with kernel-safe ARM64 GPR prfm+stnp
   streaming copy and fix vsyncFired() timer drift by subtracting present time.
4. Add 370 MHz and 465 MHz GPU_PLL0 options to lavgpuclk= and a 250 us fence
   spin in lavender_gpu_service_submit().

